  "title": "Reconcile current Product CI failure dispositions from raw lifecycle evidence",
  "status": "done",
  "milestone": null,
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1: Each added disposition names an eligible failed run, specific failure class and root cause, repair commit and a later successful, eligible Product CI run; IDs, SHA and job links are independently reproducible from the external receipt and GitHub logs.",
    "ACC-2: Recollecting the same external export produces no unexplained failure for a disposition only when its repair chain is valid. Any missing, non-later or non-successful repair remains fail-closed.",
    "ACC-3: The report still rejects long-term reliability if calendar days or eligible-run thresholds are insufficient. No failure is removed, excluded retroactively or counted as a rerun."
  ],
